<name>Power Door Lock System</name>
<para id="RM000000X28003X" category="J" type-id="3030B" name-id="622PX-00" from="200612">
<dtccode/>
<dtcname>Back door does not open</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM000000X28003X_01" type-id="33" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___000028400000">
<name>Function Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<list1 type="nonmark">
<item>
<ptxt>When the back door opener switch is pressed with the back door unlocked, the instrument panel junction block assembly (main body ECU) drives the motor in the back door lock assembly to unlatch.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
<atten3>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>The power door lock system uses large-scale body multiplex communication. First, perform the "Communication Function Inspection" according to "How to Proceed with Troubleshooting", and confirm that there is no malfunction in the communication system before proceeding with troubleshooting.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>If communication with the power window regulator master switch is interrupted (such as a disconnected connector), back door opener control is prohibited, so check that the power window system is normal.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten3>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000000X28003X_02" type-id="32" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___000028500000">
<name>Wiring Diagram</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="B159688J03" width="7.106578999in" height="3.779676365in"/>
</figure>
</content5>
</subpara>
